#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# polygonal_number

#% text
# `polygonal_number(k)` gives the `k`-th triangular number; `polygonal_number(r, k)` the `k`-th `r`-gonal number `((r - 2) k^2 - (r - 4) k)/2`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Both arguments may be symbolic, and either may be a list.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
polygonal_number(5)
#% output
#= 15

#% cell
polygonal_number(range(1, 6))
#% output
#= [1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21]

#% cell
polygonal_number(5, 3)
#% output
#= 12

#% cell
polygonal_number(r, k)
#% output
#= (1/2)*((-2 + r)*k^2 - k*(-4 + r))

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `catalan_number`, `partitions_p`
